TERMINOLOGY AND DATA SOURCES
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

NCI CTCAE v5 (Common Terminology Criteria for Adverse Events)
  - Source:  U.S. National Cancer Institute
  - Licence: U.S. Government work — public domain in the United States
  - URL:     https://ctep.cancer.gov/protocoldevelopment/electronic_applications/ctc.htm

OAE (Ontology of Adverse Events)
  - Source:  OBO Foundry
  - Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
  - Citation: He Y, Sarntivijai S, Lin Y, et al. OAE: The Ontology of Adverse Events.
              J Biomed Semantics. 2014;5:29. doi:10.1186/2041-1480-5-29

RxNorm
  - Source:  U.S. National Library of Medicine (NLM)
  - Licence: NLM Terms of Service (free for non-commercial and commercial use with attribution)
  - URL:     https://www.nlm.nih.gov/research/umls/rxnorm/
             https://lhncbc.nlm.nih.gov/RxNav/TermsofService.html
  - Required attribution (verbatim per RxNav Terms of Service):
    "This product uses publicly available data from the U.S. National Library
    of Medicine (NLM), National Institutes of Health, Department of Health and
    Human Services; NLM is not responsible for the product and does not endorse
    or recommend this or any other product."

WHO-UMC Causality Assessment Scale
  - Source:  Uppsala Monitoring Centre (WHO Programme for International Drug Monitoring)
  - Use in this project: Research and demonstration purposes only (see DISCLAIMER).
  - Note:    The WHO-UMC causality scale is referenced as a conceptual framework.
             Users and organisations should independently verify current WHO-UMC
             terms of use for their specific deployment context, particularly
             before any commercial or regulatory use.
  - URL:     https://www.who-umc.org/

FDA DailyMed Structured Product Labelling (SPL)
  - Source:  U.S. Food and Drug Administration / U.S. National Library of Medicine
  - Licence: U.S. Government work — public domain in the United States
  - URL:     https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/

Llama 3.1 (Base Model Weights)
  - Source:  Meta Platforms Inc.
  - Licence: Meta LLAMA 3 Community Licence Agreement
  - URL:     https://llama.meta.com/
  - Note:    Model weights are NOT distributed with this software. Users must
             independently download weights through Ollama under the terms of the
             Meta LLAMA 3 Community Licence.

all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (Sentence Embeddings Model)
  - Source:  UKP Lab, TU Darmstadt — distributed via Hugging Face Hub
  - Licence: Apache 2.0
  - Citation: Reimers N, Gurevych I. Sentence-BERT: Sentence Embeddings using
              Siamese BERT-Networks. EMNLP 2019. arXiv:1908.10084
  - Note:    Model weights are NOT distributed with this software. They are
             downloaded automatically by sentence-transformers on first use.

REGULATORY FRAMEWORK REFERENCES
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

ICH E2B(R3) — Electronic Standards for the Transfer of Regulatory Information
  Guideline: ICH E2B(R3), 2016.
  Publisher: International Council for Harmonisation of Technical Requirements
             for Pharmaceuticals for Human Use (ICH).

21 CFR Part 11 — Electronic Records; Electronic Signatures
  Publisher: U.S. Food and Drug Administration.

CIOMS Working Group XIV — Artificial Intelligence in Clinical Trials
  Guidance referenced for bias monitoring framework (Principle 6: demographic
  stratification of model performance).
  Publisher: Council for International Organizations of Medical Sciences (CIOMS).

ICH M2 — Electronic Standards for the Transfer of Regulatory Information
  Publisher: International Council for Harmonisation.

DISCLAIMER
━━━━━━━━━━

This software is provided for research and evaluation purposes only.
It is NOT a validated, regulatory-submission-ready pharmacovigilance system.
In particular:

  - E2B(R3) XML exports require manual MedDRA coding before submission to any
    ICH M2-compliant regulatory gateway (see governance/decisions.md ADR-001).

  - This software has NOT been validated against a labelled ICSR benchmark
    dataset (see governance/decisions.md ADR-004).

  - Users are solely responsible for ensuring compliance with applicable laws,
    regulations, and licence agreements in their jurisdiction before using this
    software in any regulated activity.
